#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:743
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to enable long double precision for &kcalc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:745
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your machine supports the C data type <type>long double</type> and if you "
"have a working libc you can enable <type>long double</type> precision for "
"&kcalc;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:749
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is what to do:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check <filename>config-kcalc.h</filename> and see whether HAVE&lowbar;"
"LONG&lowbar;DOUBLE is defined, &ie; you should be able to locate a line "
"saying:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:757
#, no-c-format
msgid "#define HAVE_LONG_DOUBLE 1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you cannot find such a line your system doesn't support long double IEEE "
"precision."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Edit the files <filename class=\"headerfile\">kcalctype.h</filename>, "
"<filename>configdlg.cpp</filename>, <filename>kcalc.cpp</filename> and "
"<filename>kcalc&lowbar;core.cpp</filename> and remove the lines:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#ifdef HAVE_LONG_DOUBLE\n"
"#undef HAVE_LONG_DOUBLE\n"
"#endif"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:771
#, no-c-format
msgid "Recompile &kcalc;."
msgstr ""

